     uurriioo — USB driver for the Rio MP3 players

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following line in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee uurriioo

     Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
     following line in loader.conf(5):

           urio_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The uurriioo driver provides support for Rio MP3 players from Diamond Multi‐
     Media which attaches to the USB port.  The uurriioo device must be configured
     in the kernel, along with _u_s_b and one of the _u_h_c_i or _o_h_c_i controllers.

     Subsequently, the _/_d_e_v_/_u_r_i_o_0 device can be used by the Rio userland ap‐
     plications.

HHAARRDDWWAARREE
     The following devices are supported by the uurriioo driver:

     ••   Diamond MultiMedia Rio 500
     ••   Diamond MultiMedia Rio 600
     ••   Diamond MultiMedia Rio 800

FFIILLEESS
     /dev/urio0
                blocking device node

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     The following line in the kernel configuration file adds the uurriioo driver
     to the kernel:
           device urio

     To download a song over the USB connection into the Rio using the
     rio_add_song(1) utility (see the _S_E_E _A_L_S_O section):
           rio_add_song /usr/local/MP3/TracyChapman/02-Fast-Car.mp3

